 "text": "The National Bureau of Standards, known today as NIST, led the federal investigation. Its engineers recovered the hanger rods and box beams, and load-tested matching connections in the laboratory. Their conclusion was stark. The load on the connection at the moment of collapse was only about thirty-one percent of what a connection designed to the Kansas City code should have been able to hold.",
